  "upload": {
    "title": "This Car Drives Sideways 🦀 #shorts",
    "description": "Hyundai Mobis' e-Corner System packs driving (in-wheel motor), braking, steering and suspension into each wheel, with no mechanical link between them, so every wheel can turn up to 90 degrees. That enables crab driving, zero turns, pivot turns and diagonal driving. In 2023 an IONIQ 5 test car with the system became the first to drive on public roads. Mobis says the technology is ready for mass production, but no production car you can buy uses it yet.",
    "hashtags": [
      "#shorts",
      "#hyundai",
      "#cars",
      "#engineering",
      "#technology"
    ]
  },
